      "content": "It sounds like you may be experiencing symptoms of acid reflux or gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). While antacids may help, it's important not to self-medicate without understanding the underlying cause. If the issue persists or worsens, I recommend consulting a healthcare professional to get an accurate diagnosis and appropriate treatment. It's essential to rule out any serious conditions. In the meantime, avoid lying down immediately after meals, try to eat smaller, more frequent meals, and avoid foods triggers like spicy or fatty foods.",
